{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA/decision before implementation: the +1/+1 bounded duplicate is not acceptable as-is because it creates a durable extra rebar ticket and Jira issue that require manual disposition. The fix will add/use a third identity signal that survives loss of both the binding-store row and the rebar-id label: Jira entity property local_id, already written during Jira create writeback. Outbound create should consult that property before creating a replacement issue and reconnect when it matches; the perturbation test will pin no duplicate growth. This honors the package-move coordination note on gunshy-symmetric-barnacle by landing at the current src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler paths before the move carries it forward."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788869202069305001,"uuid":"96c7ae46-d695-4f0a-9193-c812388a207c"}